title: "SEO Aberdeen: The Basics That Still Win in 2025"
description: "Aberdeen SMEs: get found with a fast, mobile-friendly site, people-first content, rock-solid local signals (GBP, reviews, NAP), and simple tracking. A short, fact-checked SEO guide for 2025."
publishedDate: "2025-10-10"
category: seo
---

SEO success in 2025 isn't about hacks or endless keywords — it's about doing the basics brilliantly. This guide breaks down exactly what matters for Aberdeen SMEs.

## 1) Technical Health — make the site easy to crawl

**Why it matters:** Search engines can't rank what they can't access, and users bounce from slow pages.

- **Speed / Core Web Vitals:** Target < 2.5s LCP. Fast sites help Googlebot crawl more and rank better.
- **Mobile-first:** Google indexes the mobile version first. Responsive design is non-negotiable.
- **HTTPS:** Secure sites build trust and are a page-experience signal.
- **Clean architecture:** Simple URL structure, XML sitemap, no blocked pages.
- **Error-free crawl:** Fix 4xx/5xx errors; monitor crawl stats in Search Console.

## 2) Content & Authority (E-E-A-T made practical)

**Why it matters:** Google and Bing reward pages that clearly help people and come from credible sources.

- **People-first pages:** Write for users first.
- **Natural language:** Use keywords naturally; avoid stuffing.
- **Show experience:** Include authorship, case studies, original images.
- **On-page sanity:** One H1, logical H2/H3s, clear titles and meta descriptions.

## 3) Local SEO — where Aberdeen businesses win fast

**Why it matters:** Local results (Maps/3-pack) drive calls and visits.

- **Google Business Profile (GBP):** Complete every field, add photos, post updates regularly.
- **Bing Places:** Import from Google and verify.
- **Reviews:** More and better ratings boost prominence significantly.
- **NAP consistency:** Use identical Name, Address, Phone across all citations.
- **Localised content:** Mention Aberdeen naturally; create dedicated pages for key service areas.

## 4) Structured Data — help machines understand you

- LocalBusiness schema: name, address, geo, telephone, openingHours, url
- AggregateRating/Review if you show first-party reviews
- FAQ schema for genuine Q&A sections
- Validate everything in the Rich Results Test

## 5) Measure What Matters

**Weekly checks (10 minutes):**
- Google Search Console: Queries, clicks, coverage
- GA4: Track organic engagement and conversions
- Bing Webmaster Tools: Monitor crawl, index, and backlinks

**Ignore:** meta keywords, keyword density, third-party DA/DR scores.

## 6) AI is changing the SERP — your foundations still carry you

- Fewer clicks on simple queries: AI summaries answer upfront
- Citations matter: AI highlights trustworthy sources
- Local blending: AI snapshots pull GBP data and reviews

**How to adapt:**
- Be cite-worthy: concise, structured answers with FAQ markup
- Double down on accuracy: consistent NAP, fresh hours, strong reviews
- Ship schema: feed AI parsers explicit data

